{
 "dur": 74.8,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "New York's subway",
    "runs on two steel rails.",
    "Let's take the track apart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 4.94,
   "chunks": [
    "The running rails:",
    "about 115 pounds of steel per yard,",
    "4 feet 8\u00bd inches apart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 11.62,
   "chunks": [
    "Tie plates fix them",
    "to wooden ties or concrete blocks,",
    "on ballast or concrete."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 16.87,
   "chunks": [
    "Beside them, the third rail:",
    "625 volts DC,",
    "under a cover board."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 22.45,
   "chunks": [
    "A contact shoe on the truck",
    "slides along it,",
    "to power the traction motors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 27.21,
   "chunks": [
    "The wheels aren't flat.",
    "Each tread is a slight cone,",
    "with a flange on the inside."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 32.28,
   "chunks": [
    "In a curve, the outer wheel",
    "rides its wider part",
    "and covers more ground.",
    "The train steers itself."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 38.57,
   "chunks": [
    "All that weight sits",
    "on contact patches",
    "about the size of a dime."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 42.74,
   "chunks": [
    "The wheels also",
    "short the two rails.",
    "That track circuit tells the signals",
    "a train is there."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 48.5,
   "chunks": [
    "That's why roof riding kills.",
    "Tunnel ceilings sit",
    "inches above the car.",
    "Curves and braking throw you.",
    "Below: 625 volts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 58.08,
   "chunks": [
    "Six people died subway surfing",
    "in 2024.",
    "At least five in 2025.",
    "Subway surfing kills.",
    "Don't."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v12",
   "t": 66.6,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v13",
   "t": 68.65,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "how a subway train rides its rails."
   ]
  }
 ]
